1440 [checker-scored] {"url":"/check/combo","cls":0.087,"h1":"Combo checker","disc":true,"cents":false,"hs":false,"chance":"90%","mult":"1.34x","edge":"+15 points","score":"71","drop":null,"same":null,"msg":[]}
1440 formula: Score = 50 + 250 × (our chance − price after fee) × √(past bets behind it ÷ 400, at most 1), kept between 0 and 100. 50 means the price is fair; higher means a better price than bets like this usually get; fewer past bets pull it toward 50. For a combo, the chance is each leg's chance multiplied together and the sample is the smallest leg's. That assumes the legs are independent; legs from the same event aren't.
1440 why: "Why these numbers?\n\nPays 1.16x × 1.16x = 1.34x: each leg's payout after its fee, multiplied.\n\nCombined chance 99% × 91% = 90%.\n\nScore sample: the smallest leg, about 130 similar past bets.\n\nColts vs. Texans (Texans): Model: NFL · moneyline · ~72 h · 129 eff. samples · 284 events (niche + type level)\nWill the price of Bitcoin be less than $62,000 on November 19? (No): Model: BITCOIN · multi-outcome · ~72 h · 2,717 eff. samples · 11.1K events (all markets level)"
1440 result section text: "Combined chance\n90%\nPays\n1.34x\nEdge after fee\n+15 points\nScore (of 100)\n71\n\nScore = 50 + 250 × (our chance − price after fee) × √(past bets behind it ÷ 400, at most 1), kept between 0 and 100. 50 means the price is fair; higher means a better price than bets like this usually get; fewer past bets pull it toward 50. For a combo, the chance is each leg's chance multiplied together and the sample is the smallest leg's. That assumes the legs are independent; legs from the same event aren't.\n\nWhy these numbers?\n\nPays 1.16x × 1.16x = 1.34x: each leg's payout after its fee, multiplied.\n\nCombined chance 99% × 91% = 90%.\n\nScore sample: the smallest leg, about 130 similar past bets.\n\nColts vs. Texans (Texans): Model: NFL · moneyline · ~72 h · 129 eff. samples · 284 events (niche + type level)\nWill the price of Bitcoin be less than $62,000 on November 19? (No): Model: BITCOIN · multi-outcome · ~72 h · 2,717 eff. samples · 11.1K events (all markets level)\n\n2 to 10 legs. Bet only what you can afford to lose."
